## Allowed and Prohibited Changes

### Allowed

- Rewrite `instruction.md`.
- Copy the same final text to `environment/problem_statement.md`.
- Add new tests through `tests.patch`.
- Update `tests/test.sh`, `config.json`, and `grade.py`.
- Correct `solve.sh` and `golden.patch`.
- Make only allowed Dockerfile corrections.
- Correct task metadata.
- Clean Git metadata.
- Realign `base_commit_sha` to repository HEAD when the shipped repository is the source of truth.
- Expand original PR scope when necessary and allowed.

### Prohibited

- Do not directly edit tracked source files in `environment/repo/`.
- Do not alter existing regression / pass-to-pass test files (keep them byte-identical to base).
- Do not replace or reduce PR scope.
- Do not place solution material in agent-readable paths.
- Do not add unrelated refactors.
- Do not make tests depend on live internet.
- Do not hide requirements only inside tests.

---

## Instruction Requirements

- Describe the problem, constraints, and observable outcomes — not step-by-step implementation.
- State required public schemas, formats, and contracts explicitly.
- Keep the instruction aligned with the source PR (plus any allowed expansions).
- Avoid LLM-templated or robotic phrasing.
- Avoid solution leakage (PR URLs, commit SHAs, spoilers, verifier internals).
- After any edit, copy the exact text into `environment/problem_statement.md`.

