## Test Requirements and Quality Check

Authoritative mechanical rules and auto-REMOVE patterns (silent-skip, fail-open, source-scan, wallclock, randomness, network, oracle-dep):  
`.cursor/skills/sentinel-ultra-review/reference/test-quality.md` and `check_task.py` V* findings.

Operational summary: ≥10 meaningful fail-to-pass; prefer 11–20 when claiming live “more than 10”; f2p via `tests.patch` only; never edit existing p2p files; deterministic outcome-based assertions; coverage + faithfulness both directions. Blocking Agent Judge axes ≥3.5 before Difficulty (P-010/P-011).

## Oracle and Solution Requirements

See `.cursor/skills/sentinel-ultra-review/reference/fix-playbooks.md` (oracle section) and `check_task.py` O* findings.  
`solve.sh` + `golden.patch` must satisfy the instruction without gaming, hidden goldens, or live network. Extra non-conflicting oracle functionality is OK when required behavior is implemented and tested.

## Environment Review

Fixable vs Not-Fixable environment classes: `.cursor/skills/sentinel-ultra-review/reference/environment-and-git.md`  
and `check_task.py` D*/G* findings. Dockerfile must build offline. Missing `.git` is FIXABLE (not a soft warning).

## Task Metadata Limits

Full table: `.cursor/skills/sentinel-ultra-review/reference/harbor-format.md`.  
`cpus` 2|4; `memory_mb` 2048–16384; `storage_mb` 5120–10240; `gpus` 0;  
`build_timeout_sec` ≤1800; `agent.timeout_sec` ≤**7200**; `verifier.timeout_sec` ≤1800.  
Harbor network blocks **required**: `[environment]=public`, `[agent]=allowlist` + `allowed_hosts=["api.portkey.ai"]`, `[verifier]=no-network`.  
Remove `network_mode="none"` from compose YAML if present.

## Git Repository Hygiene

Checklist and repairs: `.cursor/skills/sentinel-ultra-review/reference/environment-and-git.md` and `scripts/git_hygiene.sh`.  
HEAD must resolve and match `base_commit_sha` (shipped HEAD wins); no remotes; no filter drivers; clean tree; no reflog; `.git` <100MB; `tests.patch` must `git apply --check`. Never edit tracked repo sources during cleanup.

## Local Validation by Role

Submitter Valid-as-is: local oracle reward `1.0` and NOP `0.0` required when available.  
Submitter Fixable: strongly recommended. Reviewer: optional. Never invent rewards.

## Upload and Packaging

Zip flat contents of `task/` only (no outer `task/`, no `runs/`). Packaging sweeps and leakage:  
`.cursor/skills/sentinel-ultra-review/reference/checklists.md` and `check_task.py` P*/L3.  
Mechanical gate before Fixable upload: `python3 automation/sentinel_submitter.py static-check --task-name TASK` then `preflight`.

## Platform Evaluations

Order (Aug 4 2026): Agent Judge before Difficulty; if Judge fails, Difficulty does not run.  
Drive Judge axes ≥3.5 (esp. coverage/faithfulness). Difficulty: 4 trials/model; worse model ≤50% pass.  
Details: skill FAQ + `knowledge/patterns/P-010` / `P-011`.

## Agent-Run Analysis

Inspect all failing trials and at least one pass when available. Cite concrete logs for timeouts/misunderstandings. Smaller newer run counts are expected, not packaging defects.

## Supplemental License and Category Reference

Identify the project license when the platform asks for it. Check `environment/repo/LICENSE` (or similar), README, then upstream via `source` if needed.

### License options commonly listed on older/current platform forms

- GNU General Public License v2.0 (GPL-2.0)
- GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0)
- GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0)
- GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1 (LGPL-2.1)
- GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0 (LGPL-3.0)
- Mozilla Public License 2.0 (MPL-2.0)
- Eclipse Public License 1.0 (EPL-1.0)
- Eclipse Public License 2.0 (EPL-2.0)
- Common Public License 1.0 (CPL-1.0)
- Open Software License 3.0 (OSL-3.0)
- Reciprocal Public License 1.5 (RPL-1.5)
- Other — when more than one license applies, when there is no license, or when the license is not listed

Common licenses often mapped to **Other** when not listed: MIT, Apache 2.0, BSD 2-Clause, BSD 3-Clause, ISC, Unlicense, CC0.

### Category values (reference)

| Category | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| Fix | Fixing known bugs or faults within the codebase |
| Feature | Introducing new internal or user-oriented features |
| Refactor | Restructuring for maintainability |
| Documentation | Docs, comments, README, API docs |
| Build | Build configuration changes |
| Performance | Performance improvements |
| Chore | Housekeeping, dependency bumps, version increments |
| (Ultra free-form) | Current `task.toml` may also use other category labels (e.g. security); edit if needed for accuracy |

Use category values as reference. Prefer the labels present on the **current** platform form and in the task’s `task.toml`.

