## Legacy Compatibility Appendix

Use only for legacy packages / older forms. Prefer skill `reference/harbor-format.md` and current Ultra docs.  
Do not mix verdict names across versions. Missing `init_state.patch` alone is not a defect. Older Valid/Invalid forms map approximately to Valid as-is / Fixable / Not Fixable as in skill `reference/verdict-rubric.md`.

## Final Checklist

Before marking Valid as-is, uploading a Fixable rewrite, or accepting a submission:

- [ ] Current vs legacy structure identified; current rules applied by default
- [ ] Instruction clear, non-prescriptive, no leakage; `problem_statement.md` matches
- [ ] Source PR scope preserved (expand only; never reduce/replace)
- [ ] f2p count: official ≥10 meaningful; Fixable if <10; exactly 10 meets guideline; select live “More than 10” only when true; preferred practical 11–20; no filler tests; coverage and faithfulness both directions
- [ ] Outcome-based, deterministic tests; no silent skips / fail-open / overreach patterns
- [ ] Oracle/`golden.patch` satisfies instruction without gaming
- [ ] Environment within fixable rules or correctly marked Not Fixable
- [ ] Metadata/resources/timeouts within limits (agent ≤7200); Harbor network blocks present and correct; compose `network_mode="none"` removed if applicable
- [ ] Git hygiene clean; tracked repo sources untouched
- [ ] Packaging zip is flat `task/` contents only; no runs/; no junk artifacts
- [ ] Role-appropriate local validation completed
- [ ] Platform evals iterated until appropriate; Send to Reviewer only when ready
- [ ] Submitter and reviewer verdict systems not mixed
- [ ] Agent runs inspected (all failing trials; at least one pass when available)
- [ ] Findings cite concrete files, tests, functions, logs, and paths

